  "chain_ok": true,
  "message": "All tests pass now (2/2).\n\nThe bug was in `src/vat.js`: `withVat` used `Math.floor`, which truncates, so `withVat(999)` returned 1198 instead of 1199. The function's own comment says it should round to the nearest penny, so I changed it to `Math.round`:\n\n```js\nexports.withVat = (pence) => Math.round(pence * 1.2);\n```\n\n`pence * 1.2` can only have a fractional part in multiples of 0.2, so it never lands exactly on .5 and the rounding is unambiguous. I didn't change the test file. I haven't committed the change.",
